{"id":106097944343917,"type":"album","name":"The Last Time","artist":"The Rolling Stones","year":1965,"weight":15,"info":{"yt":"gdFQtbXAWdc","cover":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/0c9d4db3bdc435fa26793f28ea95f99a.png"},"artist_ref":{"id":44162516324628,"name":"The Rolling Stones","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/fbf4e23e89fb60e381f8e97fbf225b75/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[],"lists":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This song by The Rolling Stones served as the original source for the melody sampled in The Verve's \"Bitter Sweet Symphony.\" However, \"The Last Time\" itself was not entirely original; its core was based on a classic gospel song from the late 1950s called \"Dismay Vide Last Time\" (This May Be The Last Time). While the lyrics for \"The Last Time\" were largely derived from the gospel original, the melody was re-written by Keith Richards. Rights to this song (and other pre-1970 Rolling Stones material) were acquired by Allen Klein. \"Esa rección evidentemente viene de un próximo original de los Rolling Stones en 1965 que es de Last Time y ahí hasta donde nos remontamos a la origen de la melodía de David점 Suits Symphony.\"","year":1965,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Bitter Sweet Symphony: Quien fue su verdadero compositor?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CsBQFChCsuM"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":106097944343917,"artist":"The Rolling Stones","artist_id":44162516324628,"title":"The Last Time","year":1965,"ess":0,"yt":"gdFQtbXAWdc","kind":null,"book":{"id":1,"title":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/"},"scene":"The Rolling Stones","scene_id":44162516324628,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/#rolling-stones","chapters":["Septiembre: 7 And 7 Is: provocaciones, sombras y un nuevo lenguaje"],"pages":[[1,277]]},{"id":106097944343917,"artist":"Rolling Stones","artist